{
  "name": "JH VC MODERN (NAM)",
  "notes": "Modern, low-noise take on the late-60s wah-fuzz blues-rock tone: the Fuzz Face is replaced by a Klon-style HORSEMAN OD (much less hiss), so the gate stays gentle and notes ring out. Use your own wah pedal in front (the built-in TOUCH WAH is left off). HORSEMAN OD sits in the MOD slot as EFX, before the amp -> 1968 Super Lead NAM in slot 5 (full rig: IR off, MASTER low). SCN1 rhythm, SCN2 solo, SCN3 intro (lighter drive).",
  "order": [
    "GATE",
    "CMP",
    "EFX",
    "MOD",
    "AMP",
    "IR",
    "EQ",
    "DLY",
    "RVB",
    "PL"
  ],
